{
  "malware_family": "Medusa Ransomware (Medusa RaaS)",
  "threat_actor": "Storm-1175 (aka Spearwing); Medusa RaaS affiliates",
  "platforms": [
    "windows"
  ],
  "summary": "Medusa is a Ransomware-as-a-Service operation whose affiliates gain initial access through exploited internet-facing systems (GoAnywhere MFT, SimpleHelp, ScreenConnect, Exchange ProxyShell, Fortinet EMS) and then abuse legitimate RMM tools such as SimpleHelp, Atera and PDQ Deploy for C2, persistence and lateral movement. Encryption appends the .MEDUSA extension and drops !!!READ_ME_MEDUSA!!!.txt, while data is staged with Robocopy/Rclone and exfiltrated to endpoints such as erp.ranasons.com over ports 443/445/80. Detection should focus on unusual JWrapper/SimpleHelp agent connections, PDQ Deploy service execution of AdminArsenal payloads like gaze.exe, and large uploads to rare external hosts.",
